WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.250
Hi, I'm Hopscotch!

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:04.169
Attention can't tell where tokens are.

00:00:04.169 --> 00:00:08.009
RoPE fixes that by turning vectors like the hands of a clock.

00:00:09.808 --> 00:00:13.703
Rotate each query and key by an angle that grows with its position.

00:00:13.703 --> 00:00:17.299
Then the angle between them, and their score, depends only on how

00:00:17.299 --> 00:00:18.498
far apart they are.

00:00:20.008 --> 00:00:23.534
In every layer, each token's hidden state is projected to a query

00:00:23.534 --> 00:00:25.003
and a key, as usual.

00:00:25.423 --> 00:00:27.451
Split each head's dimensions into pairs.

00:00:27.451 --> 00:00:30.830
Each pair turns by the position times its own angle.

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:34.730
Dot a turned query with a turned key, and only the difference

00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:35.890
in their positions survives.

00:00:36.310 --> 00:00:37.517
Values are never rotated.

00:00:37.517 --> 00:00:39.327
RoPE has no weights at all.

00:00:41.192 --> 00:00:42.297
Here's the whole proof.

00:00:43.192 --> 00:00:45.202
Turn the query by its position, m.

00:00:46.433 --> 00:00:48.134
Turn the key by its position, n.

00:00:49.674 --> 00:00:53.480
Undo one turn and apply the other, and what's left is a

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:55.383
single turn by n minus m.

00:00:55.383 --> 00:00:56.335
Absolute position cancels.

00:00:57.758 --> 00:01:01.953
With base ten thousand, eighteen of the sixty-four pairs never finish a

00:01:01.953 --> 00:01:03.701
turn in four thousand tokens.

00:01:03.701 --> 00:01:06.848
Longer inputs show them angles the model never saw.

00:01:08.525 --> 00:01:14.842
Position interpolation divides every position, so all angles stay familiar, but neighbours crowd together.

00:01:15.262 --> 00:01:19.704
NTK-aware scaling raises the base instead, so only the slow pairs stretch.

00:01:20.124 --> 00:01:24.086
YaRN decides pair by pair: stretch the slow ones, keep the fast

00:01:24.086 --> 00:01:25.407
ones, and blend between.

00:01:25.827 --> 00:01:27.739
Or train with a bigger base.

00:01:27.739 --> 00:01:29.651
Llama 3 uses five hundred thousand.

00:01:31.142 --> 00:01:33.064
RoPE turns position into rotation.

00:01:33.064 --> 00:01:37.676
Attention reads relative distance for free, and long context becomes a question

00:01:37.676 --> 00:01:40.366
of which angles the model has seen.

00:01:41.858 --> 00:01:44.540
Rotate, subtract, and keep the angles familiar.

00:01:46.458 --> 00:01:48.620
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:49.237
I'm Hopscotch.

00:01:49.237 --> 00:01:49.546
Bye!
